   <property name="text">
    <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Instructions:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Drag the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Sugarcane Juice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; into the pot, then click the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Boil&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; button to create molasses.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Did you know?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Molasses is a thick, dark syrup left over after extracting sugar from sugarcane juice. For every 100 tons of sugarcane processed, about 3 to 5 tons of molasses are produced. Rich in residual sugars and minerals, molasses serves as the primary ingredient in about 90% of the world’s rum. It not only fuels fermentation but also contributes to the deep, robust flavors found in traditional rums across the Caribbean and beyond.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
